    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This paper summarizes previous findings regarding the relations of several Miocene age sedimentary basins to two major faults, the Las Vegas shear zone and the Bitter Spring Valley fault, it also describes and analyzes the patterns, spatial distributions, and sequence of joints, pressure solution surfaces,folds, and faults within these basins adjacent to the major faults. The structural patterns and the spatial-temporal relationships suggest that these secondary structures are associated with the slip on the major faults. The observed dependence of type and geometric patterns of various structures to lithology is also presented.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
